You lose items before you get to choose which ones to remove.

Suppose the bag has 150 items (a bit over 6 pages, with normal window 
size), and that the OP isn't willing to strip completely, so has 45 
inventory slots available.

He'll lose (expected) 11.5 items on first loot, call it 12.  Then 
remove 45, 93 left.  Loot it again, lose 7 items, remove 45 more.  At 
that point he can probably pick the bag up to uncurse, and if not 
that's fine, since what's left is probably low value anyway.  If he 
already has a BOH, it might not even be worth spending a potion of holy 
water just to save a few stacks of food from vanishing.





